#{\footnote what_is}${\footnote What BASILISK 16 Is}+{\footnote main:020}K{\footnote BASILISK 16;about;Sound Recorder;Windows 3.11;emulator;machine}
\pard\keepn\sb120\sa120\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs24\b What BASILISK 16 Is\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 BASILISK 16 is a plugin instrument for a {\ul DAW}{\v term_daw}. It is a VST3 for Windows and macOS, and also an Audio Unit on macOS.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Each copy of the plugin runs its own Windows 3.11 in an emulator. In that Windows, sixteen copies of Sound Recorder (SOUNDREC.EXE) are open. The plugin calls each copy a {\ul recorder}{\v term_recorder}.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 When you play a note, the plugin chooses a recorder. That Sound Recorder plays its sound through the sound card of Windows 3.11, at the pitch of your note. The plugin passes that sound to your DAW. It does not make a sound of its own.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The sound itself is one line of text, the {\ul DNA}{\v term_dna}. Windows builds it with Sound Recorder's own menu commands: Increase Speed, Add Echo, Reverse, Paste Mix and the rest.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b See Also\par
\pard\sa30\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb Playing the Instrument}{\v playing}\par
\pard\sa30\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb The DNA}{\v dna}\par
\page
#{\footnote playing}${\footnote Playing the Instrument}+{\footnote main:030}K{\footnote playing;MIDI;notes;velocity;sustain pedal;pitch bend;mod wheel;parameters;automation;latency}
\pard\keepn\sb120\sa120\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs24\b Playing the Instrument\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Put BASILISK 16 on an instrument track and play. When the plugin loads, Windows starts and the sixteen recorders arrange themselves into one instrument. This takes a few seconds.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b What the plugin hears\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Notes\tab Each note plays on one or more recorders, at its own pitch.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Velocity\tab How hard you play sets the volume. See the {\ul Velocity}{\v term_velocity} setting.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Sustain pedal\tab Holds notes after you let go of the keys.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Pitch bend\tab Bends notes by up to the Bend Range. The bend is set when a note starts.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Mod wheel\tab Adds to Macro 1. See {\uldb Macros and the Mod Wheel}{\v macros}.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Parameters in your DAW\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 These can be automated:\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Attack, Decay\tab Times in milliseconds.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Sustain\tab Level in percent.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Release\tab Time in milliseconds.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Velocity\tab How much velocity changes the volume.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Bend Range\tab The pitch bend range in semitones.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Transpose\tab Moves every note, in semitones.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Output Gain\tab The output level in dB.\par
\pard\sa30\li1555\ri175\fi-1440\tx1555\plain\f0\fs20 Macro 1 to 4\tab Whatever the sound maps them to.\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Each parameter is part of the DNA. When you change one, the DNA changes too, and your project saves it.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Timing\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The plugin tells your DAW its latency (60 ms), so recorded notes play back in time. When you play live, you hear the delay.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b See Also\par
\pard\sa30\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb The Keyboard, Bend and Mod Wheel}{\v keyboard}\par
\pard\sa30\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb Presets}{\v presets}\par
