#{\footnote effects}${\footnote Effects and Edits}+{\footnote main:080}K{\footnote steps;Effects;Edit;Increase Volume;Decrease Volume;Increase Speed;Decrease Speed;Add Echo;Reverse;Copy;Paste Insert;Paste Mix;Insert File;Mix with File;Delete Before;Delete After;position}
\pard\keepn\sb120\sa120\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs24\b Effects and Edits\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 Each {\ul step}{\v term_step} of a layer is one of Sound Recorder's own commands. The commands run in order on that layer's sound.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Effects\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 +}\tab Increase Volume (by 25%)\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 -}\tab Decrease Volume\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 >}\tab Increase Speed (by 100%): half as long, an octave up\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 <}\tab Decrease Speed: twice as long, an octave down\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 E}\tab Add Echo\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 R}\tab Reverse\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Edits\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 @}{\i NN}\tab Move the position to NN% of the length (0 to 99)\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 @t}{\i N}\tab Move the position to N milliseconds\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 [}\tab Delete Before Current Position\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 ]}\tab Delete After Current Position\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 C}\tab Copy the whole sound\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 P}\tab Paste Insert at the position\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 X}\tab Paste Mix at the position\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 I}{\i name}\tab Insert File: insert that sound at the position\par
\pard\sa30\li1215\ri175\fi-1100\tx1215\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 M}{\i name}\tab Mix with File: mix that sound in at the position\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 The position starts at 0 when the source sound loads. If {\f1 P} or {\f1 X} comes before any {\f1 C}, they paste the layer's source sound.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b Example\par
\pard\sa60\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\f1 tada@20[} keeps tada.wav from 20% to the end: it moves to 20%, then deletes what comes before.\par
\pard\sb115\sa25\li115\ri175\plain\f0\fs20\b See Also\par
\pard\sa30\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb Collages}{\v collages}\par
\pard\sa30\li395\ri175\plain\f0\fs20 {\uldb The Sounds}{\v sounds}\par
